Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0094L=LAMBERT - Good job Fisher. I'll inform the Joint Chiefs that Lacerda is no longer a threat.
Speech_0099L=REDDING - Fisher, we can't extract you until you complete your primary objectives.
Speech_0100L=FISHER - Alright. I'll double back.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0003L=LAMBERT - Good job Fisher. I'll inform the Joint Chiefs that Lacerda is no longer a threat. Your primaries objectives are completed. We can extract you whenever you're ready.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0097L=LAMBERT - Fisher, Lacerda is in the Captain's quarters. Third deck, port side. Use the interior stairwells.
Speech_0098L=LAMBERT - Fisher, the Captain might have logged a record of Lacerda's room assignment on the ships server. Check the top deck to find out where Lacerda is.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0047L=LAMBERT - That's their alarm system Fisher... I'm warning you... be careful
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0048L=LAMBERT - Fisher... be careful... if you put the whole ship on alert, you'll regret it.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0049L=LAMBERT - Dammit Fisher, you're a liability.
Speech_0050L=FISHER - It's just another alarm...
Speech_0051L=LAMBERT - It's more than that. The whole ship is alerted. Complete your primary objectives and forget the rest.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0052L=LAMBERT - Dammit Fisher, you just kicked the hornets nest. The whole ship is on alert.
Speech_0053L=LAMBERT - Fisher, the ship has a central alarm system. If you set off too many alarms, they'll know you're there and your life will be a lot more difficult.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0112L=Officials in Peru have confirmed the recovery of the body of American Computer Engineer Bruce Morgenholt. No cause of death has yet been announced, but the State Department has demanded an apology from the Peruvian Army for their possible role in a botched rescue operation.
Speech_0113L=In Japan, Admiral Toshiro Otomo publicly revealed I-SDF findings relating to events leading up to 'Black Gold Da'. The I-SDF report alleges that North Korean and Chinese information warfare attacks may have manipulated worldwide markets to bring about the economic collapse in Japan.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0114L=LAMBERT - Information you recovered in Peru makes it look like Hugo Lacerda was contracted by a third party to kidnap and interrogate Morgenholt. His payment was in weapons. He appears to be using those arms to equip his own men, and pay off debts to other guerilla groups. Maybe Lacerda is a nickel-ante loser... but maybe he learned things from Morgenholt that we don't want anyone to know. The Maria Narcissa is out to sea, so there's no escape. Board her, search her, find out who Lacerda has been dealing with, and then make sure he doesn't have an opportunity to spread what he knows. Fifth Freedom.
Speech_0115L=GRIMSDOTTIR - What Morgenholt knew about the Masse Kernels, recursive computation and weaponized algorithms is akin to what Oppenheimer knew about atoms, or what Turing knew about digital computers. Project Watson... the United Nations investigation into the Masse Kernels will be remembered for centuries alongside the Manhattan Project as fundamental research that changed the nature of warfare forever. Imagine if Che Guevara had kidnapped and interrogated Oppenhiemer in 1959 and you have a pretty accurate parallel of the situation we're in right now.
Speech_0116L=REDDING - We're going to send the helicopter out about forty clicks ahead of the Maria Narcissa and leave you in the water on her course. You'll board covertly onto the bow. Search the ship and the holds. Find out what you can about the arms shipments and who Lacerda is dealing with. Satellite imaging shows the Maria Narcissa racks a small launch on the stern. That will be your primary extraction. If everything goes bad, we might be able to arrange to pluck you out of the sea.
Speech_0117L=PARTRIDGE - We'll keep the Walsh inside of helicopter range of the target vessel at all times. If something goes wrong, we should be able to assist in extraction. If you play it safe, we'll recover you in the ships launch from open water once you're out of visual range of the ship.

[P_02_CargoShip_MachineShopSailor]

[P_02_CargoShip_MemorableM]
POPUPMESSAGE_0028=Eliminate Hugo Lacerda.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=LACERDA - I tell you... never... never in my life have I been so insult!
Speech_0018L=Damien - I don't see why you're upset. He got you past the inspection. You think it's easy to get through the Canal Zone with all the crackdowns these days?
Speech_0003L=LACERDA - I don't care if it's hard! You think my job is easy? No! But this insult! Forcing me to bribe an inspector! Out of my own pocket! No! This big shot... this Vice President Senor Segundo Ruiz de Medeiros... ha! I'll show him.
Speech_0021L=Damien - Fine.
Speech_0004L=LACERDA - Mark my words! I'll make him pay! I'll make him pay double! Or my name is not Hugo Lacerda!
Speech_0022L=Damien - Great.
Speech_0008L=LACERDA - I need another drink.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0009L=LACERDA - Let me see...
Speech_0017L=LACERDA - Now where would that fat pig stash his rum...
Speech_0011L=LACERDA - Ahh... bastard... I want rum...
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0012L=LACERDA - Si, si... fine... as soon as I find it... must be here somewhere.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0013L=LACERDA - What do I look like? A damn waiter? Ha!
Speech_0014L=LACERDA - Hmm... let's see.
Speech_0024L=Damien - So...?
Speech_0015L=LACERDA - Bastard doesn't have any liquor.
Speech_0020L=Norman - What about my beer?
Speech_0016L=LACERDA - Shut up...
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0025L=Damien - Lacerda, come on... bring us a drink!
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0026L=Damien - What, you need a hand?
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0027L=Damien - C'mon Lacerda... hurry up...

[P_02_CargoShip_MessHallSoldiers]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=Kemen - Hey, Tomas, have you seen Lacerda?
Speech_0004L=Tomas - No... but I heard him yelling at someone a few minutes ago. That's why I came here.
Speech_0002L=Kemen - What was he yelling about this time.
Speech_0005L=Tomas - Complaining about his quarters or something.
Speech_0003L=Kemen - Bastard... thinks now that he's got a little cash he's the king of the world.
Speech_0006L=Tomas - He'll get his one of these days. You'll see.

[P_02_CargoShip_Objectives]
Objective_0001=Retrieve the bill of lading for Lacerda's arms shipment.
Objective_0024=The arms used to pay Lacerda were shipped in a large crate, located in one of the cargo holds. Locate and read the Bill of Lading, mounted on the side of the crate.
Objective_0003=Retrieve the ship's transit ledger for Lacerda's shipment.
Objective_0025=A computerized ledger will be kept in the ship's office. Access this ledger to determine who facilitated the delivery of the arms to Lacerda.
Objective_0018=Eliminate Hugo Lacerda.
Objective_0026=Hugo Lacerda has been elevated to Third Echelon's Target of Opportunity list. Take advantage of any possible opportunity to remove him from the list.
Objective_0008=Find the name of Lacerda's Panamanian contact.
Objective_0027=In addition to those shipping and receiving the weapons, someone must also have helped Lacerda get them past new security inspection protocols at the Panama Canal. Find out who.
POPUPMESSAGE_0061=Retrieve the bill of lading for Lacerda's arms shipment.
Objective_0019=Place tracking devices on any illegal weapons crates.
Objective_0028=Planting tracking devices on the remaining crates that Lacerda is delivering to his allies and supporters may assist in future intelligence operations.
POPUPMESSAGE_0062=Place tracking devices on any illegal weapons crates.
Objective_0020=Find out which cabin Lacerda is in.
Objective_0029=Interrogate the Captain, or check the ship's register in the main computer room to find out which room Lacerda is in.
