[P_02_CargoShip_TopDeckSoldiers]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=PrGeu_A - What does it mean 'to bootstrap'?
Speech_0006L=PrGeu_B - Uh...it means 'to accomplish something by using an entirely internal process...' why?
Speech_0002L=PrGeu_A - Ay... the Americans say they will have to 'bootstrap' a shuttle launch if they want to save the astronauts on the ISS.
Speech_0007L=PrGeu_B - It's that bad?
Speech_0003L=PrGeu_A - It's worse... they say that since the wreckage of the first shuttle is still attached to the docking module, the crew will need to space walk to the rescue shuttle...
Speech_0008L=PrGeu_B - ...that doesn't sound good...
Speech_0004L=PrGeu_A - Well, it will be two weeks before they can even launch the shuttle, so it might not even matter...
Speech_0009L=PrGeu_B - And I thought this ship was dangerous...
Speech_0005L=PrGeu_A - This ship isn't moving at thirty thousand kilometers an hour.

